# SymbiYosys job for the SECDED (72, 64) weight-SRAM codec.
#
#   sby -f secded.sby bmc      full proof of the property set (boolector)
#   sby -f secded.sby bmc_abc  the same proof on an independent engine
#   sby -f secded.sby cover    non-vacuity of every property branch
#
# The properties live in formal/secded_props.v, a wrapper module that
# composes hw/rtl/secded_enc.v with hw/rtl/secded_dec.v and drives them
# with a symbolic data word and a symbolic 72-bit error vector
# ($anyconst). Both modules are purely combinational, so BMC at depth 1
# evaluates the entire input space: this is a full proof in the sense of
# docs/09-formal-verification-plan.md target #2 ("UNSAT at depth 1 covers
# the whole input space"), not a bounded result.
#
# Engine diversity (docs/09 section C.4 item 7) is expressed as two tasks
# rather than two engines in one task: sby races the engines listed inside
# a task and reports the first to answer, so a second engine there would
# be a speed hedge, not independent confirmation. The two tasks use
# different engine families - an SMT bit-blaster (boolector) and the
# AIGER/SAT path (abc bmc3) - so a solver-specific defect would have to
# occur twice to go unnoticed.
#
# Engine choice is measured, not inherited: on this query boolector closes
# in about 17 s and abc bmc3 in about 10 s, while yices (the engine the
# aer_fifo job uses) had not returned after 3 minutes. bitwuzla, at about
# 19 s, is an equivalent alternative to boolector.
#
# The property set has since grown by the two check-port assertions C1/C2
# and the second decoder instance they need (see secded_props.v). That did
# not change the engine ranking: two re-measured runs reported 7 and 10 CPU
# seconds for bmc against 2 and 3 for bmc_abc, in formal/secded_bmc/status
# and formal/secded_bmc_abc/status [fact, two runs, machine under other
# load - an order of magnitude, not a benchmark].
#
# There is deliberately no `mode prove` task. The design has no state - the
# only registers in the model are the two $anyconst inputs - so k-induction
# has nothing to induct over and BMC at depth 1 is already exhaustive. The
# voter, which is equally stateless but far smaller, keeps a prove task in
# formal/tmr_voter.sby as a cheap cross-check of that reasoning.

[tasks]
bmc
bmc_abc
cover

[options]
bmc: mode bmc
bmc: depth 1
bmc_abc: mode bmc
bmc_abc: depth 1
cover: mode cover
cover: depth 1

[engines]
bmc: smtbmc boolector
bmc_abc: abc bmc3
cover: smtbmc boolector

[script]
read_verilog -formal secded_enc.v
read_verilog -formal secded_dec.v
read_verilog -formal secded_props.v
prep -top secded_props

[files]
../hw/rtl/secded_enc.v
../hw/rtl/secded_dec.v
secded_props.v
